From a712db9f3a4e2cf9361a3a1f270c4b3205724870 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:05:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Switch InfluxDB auth to username/password, matching BESS
 Manager
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Home Energy Manager's InfluxDB connection required a v2 API token
(org+token, Flux over /api/v2/query) that was never actually set up —
the container logs showed "Historical Data Access: NOT_CONFIGURED" all
day, leaving today's Cost & Savings entirely synthetic (0 of 96 periods
recorded as "actual", vs. BESS Manager's 63/96) even though BESS Manager
already reads the same InfluxDB v2 server successfully.

BESS Manager uses InfluxDB's built-in v1-compatibility login instead
(username+password, InfluxQL over /query) — simpler to obtain than a v2
API token and already proven working. Rewrote influxdb_helper.py to use
the same approach so the already-working BESS Manager credentials can be
copied straight into this app's Configuration tab, and updated
config.yaml's schema to match.

Bumped to v0.1.15.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9yfcLt9RHbqoZD18y9PT7
